s":"we shall do"},{"surface":"கொல்","parts":[{"text":"கொல்","lemma":"kol","gloss":"particle of doubt"}],"gloss":"particle of doubt"},{"surface":"தோழி","parts":[{"text":"தோழி","lemma":"tōḻi","gloss":"friend"}],"gloss":"O friend"},{"surface":"நோதக","parts":[{"text":"நோ","lemma":"nō","gloss":"pain"},{"text":"தக","lemma":"taka","gloss":"so as to fit"}],"gloss":"painfully"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நீர்","parts":[{"text":"நீர்","lemma":"nīr","gloss":"water"}],"gloss":"water"},{"surface":"எதிர்","parts":[{"text":"எதிர்","lemma":"etir","gloss":"receive"}],"gloss":"receiving"},{"surface":"கருவிய","parts":[{"text":"கருவி","lemma":"karuvi","gloss":"cloud"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"adjectival suffix"}],"gloss":"having clouds"},{"surface":"கார்","parts":[{"text":"கார்","lemma":"kār","gloss":"rainy season"}],"gloss":"rainy season"},{"surface":"எதிர்","parts":[{"text":"எதிர்","lemma":"etir","gloss":"face"}],"gloss":"facing"},{"surface":"கிளை","parts":[{"text":"கிளை","lemma":"kiḷai","gloss":"group"}],"gloss":"group of"},{"surface":"மழை","parts":[{"text":"மழை","lemma":"maḻai","gloss":"clouds"}],"gloss":"clouds"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஊதை","parts":[{"text":"ஊதை","lemma":"ūtai","gloss":"cold north wind"}],"gloss":"cold north wind"},{"surface":"அம்","parts":[{"text":"அம்","lemma":"am","gloss":"euphonic increment"}],"gloss":"euphonic increment"},{"surface":"குளிரொடு","parts":[{"text":"குளிர்","lemma":"kuḷir","gloss":"coldness"},{"text":"ஒடு","lemma":"oṭu","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with coldness"},{"surface":"பேதுற்று","parts":[{"text":"பேது","lemma":"pētu","gloss":"confusion"},{"text":"உற்று","lemma":"uṟu","gloss":"having experienced"}],"gloss":"having become bewildered"},{"surface":"மயங்கிய","parts":[{"text":"மயங்கு","lemma":"mayaṅku","gloss":"be confused"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"iya","gloss":"past relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"which is confused"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கூதிர்","parts":[{"text":"கூதிர்","lemma":"kūtir","gloss":"cold season"}],"gloss":"cold season"},{"surface":"உருவின்","parts":[{"text":"உருவு","lemma":"uruvu","gloss":"form"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"of the form"},{"surface":"கூற்றம்","parts":[{"text":"கூற்றம்","lemma":"kūṟṟam","gloss":"God of Death"}],"gloss":"God of Death"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"காதலர்","parts":[{"text":"காதலர்","lemma":"kātalar","gloss":"lover"}],"gloss":"lover"},{"surface":"பிரிந்த","parts":[{"text":"பிரி","lemma":"piri","gloss":"separate"},{"text":"ந்த","lemma":"nta","gloss":"past relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"who separated"},{"surface":"என்","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"yāṉ","gloss":"me"}],"gloss":"me"},{"surface":"குறித்து","parts":[{"text":"குறி","lemma":"kuṟi","gloss":"aim"},{"text":"த்து","lemma":"ttu","gloss":"having done"}],"gloss":"aiming at"},{"surface":"வருமே","parts":[{"text":"வரு","lemma":"varu","gloss":"come"},{"text":"ம்","lemma":"m","gloss":"habitual suffix"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"comes indeed"}]}],"literal":"What shall we do, O friend, painfully? / Water-receiving, cloud-laden, rainy-season-facing, group of clouds, / with the cold north wind and chilliness, having become bewildered and confused, / the God of Death in the form of the cold season, / aiming at me who is separated from my lover, comes indeed!","translation":"What shall we do, my friend? Painfully, the God of Death, taking the form of this cold season—confused and bewildered by the cold north wind, the chilliness, and the swarms of water-laden clouds that face the rainy season—comes indeed, aiming at me, who am separated from my lover.","modern":"தோழி! நாம் என்ன செய்வோம்? வருத்தம் தரும்படியாக, நீரை ஏற்றுக்கொண்ட மேகக் கூட்டங்கள் கார்ப்பருவத்தை எதிர்நோக்கி, வாடைக் காற்றோடும் குளிரோடும் கூடி, மயக்கமடைந்து விளங்கும் இக்கூதிர் காலத்தின் வடிவத்தைக் கொண்ட எமன், என் காதலரைப் பிரிந்து வாழும் என்னை நோக்கி வருகிறானே!","explanation":"In this poem, the heroine speaks to her close friend in deep distress. Her lover has gone away, and the cold season (kūtir) has arrived in his absence, bringing freezing winds and dark clouds. Instead of just a seasonal change, the heroine perceives the cold season as Yama, the God of Death, coming to end her life. The imagery of the cold north wind (ūtai) and the water-laden clouds (maḻai) heightens her sense of isolation and vulnerability. This poem belongs to the Neytal tiṇai, which beautifully captures the mood of pining and despair in separation.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,1.1],[1.1,1.3],[1.3,1.7],[1.7,3.1],[3.1,3.1],[3.1,3.2],[3.3,3.6],[3.98,5.5],[5.5,6.0],[6.0,6.4],[6.4,6.5],[6.5,7.4],[7.4,7.7],[7.7,7.9],[7.9,9.4],[9.4,9.7],[9.83,10.2],[10.2,10.5]],"female":[[0.0,0.63],[0.7,1.1],[1.1,1.5],[1.5,1.8],[1.8,3.0],[3.0,3.0],[3.0,3.08],[3.16,3.4],[3.82,5.5],[5.5,6.0],[6.0,6.5],[6.5,6.6],[6.6,7.9],[7.9,8.2],[8.2,8.4],[8.4,9.85],[9.85,10.15],[10.2,10.8],[10.8,11.1]]}}